title: 6th World International Congress of the Comintern
subtitle: Maintain the united front?
tags: event, govt_affairs
is-card: true
on-arrival: comintern_seen = 1
view-if: comintern_seen = 0 and year = 1928 and month >= 9
new-page: true
face-image: img/comintern.jpg

= 6th International Congress

The major debate during this meeting is the matter of the united front. Many believe it to be unecessary as we are in a "third period" of capitalism where its collapse is imminent, as shown by the economic crises of the last few years. 

- @maintain_united_front: Keep the united front! If fascism arises, we will be glad we have allies.
- @third_period_thesis: Adopt the Third Period thesis! The social fascists cannot be trusted.

@maintain_united_front
on-arrival: left_opposition_dissent += 10; marxist_leninists_dissent += 10; conciliators_strength += 10; right_opposition_strength -= 10; spd_relation +=10
choose-if: united_front_support >=3 and comintern_relation >=0
unavailable-subtitle: The united front currently lacks support.

Through our influence, the united front is retained. Many are opposed to this but democratic centralism puts them in line soon enough.

@third_period_thesis
on-arrival: spd_relation -=15; united_front_maintained -=1;conciliators_strength -= 10; right_opposition_strength -= 10

Capitalism's collaspe is imminent, the Third Period thesis will be adopted. Any further cooperation with the SPD will be criticised by our party and the Comintern, if not entirely rejected.
